# PicoVolt Proprietary Lifetime License 1.0

**Prepared edition 1.0 — 11 September 2026.** This becomes an offer only when
an official release notice identifies the Licensor, covered release, exact terms
and fee. No proprietary engine release is currently offered under these terms.
Previously released Apache-licensed components retain their existing licenses.

## 1. Parties and acceptance

“Licensor” is **BEYOND SOFTWARE S.R.L.**, a Romanian company, CUI **40707869**,
with its published registered address at **Str. Fabricii nr. 11, ap. 16,
Cluj-Napoca, Cluj, 400620, Romania**. Contact: **contact@beyond-software.ro**.
The release notice must repeat the then-current contracting details before acceptance.
“You” means the accepting
individual or the organization they are authorized to represent. “Software” means
only the proprietary components and exact versions identified in that notice.

You must be able to read and save these terms before delivery. Checking an
initially unchecked acceptance box and clicking **Accept license and download**
records acceptance for the identified release. For automated downloads, an
authorized account administrator may first accept these same identified terms
and issue scoped credentials. Visiting a page, receiving a file, or downloading
an old Apache release does not constitute acceptance of this agreement.

The release notice identifies the legal party, product/version, artifact digest,
license version/digest, customer category and price including applicable taxes
(or explicitly zero). No unpublished fee or usage limit applies. Any paid grant
is subject to the payment conditions disclosed before acceptance. You must
receive a durable copy of the accepted terms and receipt. If you decline, do not
obtain or use proprietary releases under this offer; independently held licenses
and existing Apache rights are unaffected.

## 2. Perpetual license

Subject to these terms and payment of any stated one-time fee, Licensor grants a
worldwide, non-exclusive, perpetual license to install, run and back up the covered
Software for personal and internal business purposes and to build and operate
your own applications. There is no per-query charge, device limit or recurring
license renewal unless separately negotiated in writing before acceptance.

“Lifetime” means indefinite use of the covered versions, including if Licensor
ceases trading, subject only to section 8. It does not mean the lifetime of an
account, server or subscription. Lawfully obtained copies remain usable offline
without periodic activation. Ending Hub service does not end this engine grant.

You may modify source supplied to you for permitted use. Employees and contractors
may act on your behalf under equivalent confidentiality/use restrictions; you
remain responsible for them. Affiliates are not automatically separate licensees.
A merger or sale of substantially all the relevant business may transfer this
license with that business if the successor assumes these obligations and you
retain no separate right to use transferred copies.

## 3. Commercial application embedding

You may distribute object-code copies embedded in applications whose principal
purpose is other than providing a general-purpose database engine, database SDK,
or managed database/dataset-distribution platform. Product catalogs, editors,
games, business analytics and inventory applications are examples. Charging for
these applications is permitted. Customers may run the embedded engine offline.

Retain copyright, license and third-party notices. Supply end-user terms allowing
operation and backup of the embedded component within your application while
protecting it from standalone redistribution. End users' rights in lawfully
distributed copies survive termination of your license unless they independently
breach applicable terms. No broader standalone engine or source sublicense is
granted. Your application code and datasets remain yours.

## 4. Reserved rights

“Competing Database Product” means a product whose principal customer-facing
function is providing a general-purpose database engine, database SDK, hosted
database, or managed distribution of independently supplied database datasets.
An application does not become a Competing Database Product merely because it
stores data, offers search, exports user data, serves its own catalogs, or uses
the Software as one component of a broader product.

Without a separate written agreement, you may not:

1. sell, rent, sublicense, redistribute or offer proprietary Software as a
   standalone database engine or SDK, or as a Competing Database Product;
2. offer third parties a general-purpose hosted database or managed immutable
   dataset-distribution platform built on proprietary Software where that engine
   or platform is the principal product being sold;
3. distribute proprietary source or modified proprietary engines, except
   confidential access by your permitted contractors;
4. remove ownership notices, claim the Software as your own, or suggest official
   PicoVolt sponsorship through names/logos without permission; or
5. bypass delivery controls to obtain proprietary releases without entitlement.

These restrictions do not prohibit independent competing implementations, use
of your own data, truthful benchmarks, security research, or rights under an
independently obtained Apache license. They do not restrict reverse engineering
or interoperability to the extent mandatory law protects those activities.

Operating your own application for customers, including a paid SaaS application,
is permitted under section 3 when that application is not a Competing Database
Product. A hosted catalog that serves your application's own users is permitted;
a general-purpose service that sells database hosting or dataset distribution
to unrelated application developers requires a separate agreement. No provision
restricts competition using software independently developed or licensed to you.

## 5. Ownership and third-party rights

Licensor and contributors retain ownership of their Software. You retain your
data, application code and modifications you author, subject to these terms for
the underlying Software. No ownership of customer data transfers to Licensor.

To the extent controlled by Licensor, this grant includes patent rights necessarily
infringed by permitted use of covered Software, excluding claims arising only from
your additions or combinations. No trademark rights are granted beyond truthful
component identification. Third-party notices must accompany releases and their
licenses prevail for their components. Existing Apache grants are not narrowed.

## 6. Updates and support

The perpetual grant covers releases identified in your receipt plus updates
expressly added to it. It does not promise future major releases, indefinite
maintenance, an SLA, hosting, bandwidth, storage or support. Later terms may be
accepted or declined without changing the license for versions already obtained.

Support requires applicable license acceptance and, where specified, a separate
support agreement. Acceptance alone purchases no SLA. Existing written commitments
and mandatory obligations prevail. Release notes must explain compatibility and
migration boundaries. Nothing authorizes disabling older installations, deleting
user data or preventing export because new terms are declined.

## 7. Hub and privacy

Hub is separately subscribed hosted software. Service, privacy, data processing,
retention, cancellation and export terms must be provided before activation.
This license grants no lifetime hosting and is not marketing or analytics consent.

Local engine use requires no telemetry. Entitlement records are limited to what
is necessary to record the parties, license, artifacts, acceptance and payment;
purposes and retention must be disclosed before collection. Optional analytics
require a separate choice where applicable.

## 8. Termination

You may terminate by ceasing use and removing proprietary copies, retaining any
copy mandatory law requires. Licensor may terminate only for a material breach
uncured 30 days after written notice describing it, or immediately when a court
order or mandatory law requires. There is no termination for convenience,
inactivity, subscription cancellation or refusal of later terms.

After valid termination, stop using/distributing affected proprietary Software,
except for a 30-day read/export period solely to recover your own data where
legally permitted. Existing Apache grants, independent licenses and section 3
end-user rights survive. No remote interference with systems or data is authorized.

## 9. Warranties and liability

Except for express written warranties and non-excludable rights, Software is
supplied as available without warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose or uninterrupted operation. Keep independent backups and
evaluate suitability for your application.

To the extent permitted by law, neither party is liable under this license for
indirect or consequential losses. Each party's aggregate liability is limited to
the greater of EUR 500 and all fees paid for the affected Software license.
These limits do not cover fraud, deliberate misconduct, gross negligence, death
or personal injury caused by negligence, or liability that cannot lawfully be
limited. Separate service agreements may allocate service liability without
reducing mandatory rights.

## 10. General and mandatory protections

These terms and the accepted release notice form the Software agreement.
Additional written agreements apply to their identified scope. Changing an
existing grant requires mutual agreement; posting new website terms is not enough.
An unenforceable provision is severed only to the extent necessary. Remaining
terms continue where legally possible. Non-enforcement is not a permanent waiver.

Mandatory consumer, competition, privacy, accessibility, interoperability and
statutory update rights prevail. Consumer checkout must supply required
disclosures, withdrawal information and separate express consents. This document
does not waive those rights. Romanian law governs this agreement. For business
customers, disputes fall within the competent courts of Cluj-Napoca, Romania,
subject to mandatory jurisdiction rules. Consumers retain the protections of
mandatory law in their habitual residence and any right to bring proceedings
before their home courts. Nothing in this choice of law removes those protections.

## Activation record

This edition is prepared for the owner's release process. Before issuing a proprietary release,
verify the current Licensor details and complete the rights inventory, release manifest,
price/customer scope, acceptance/receipt service and statutory disclosures.
Do not present unissued terms as an executed license. Qualified legal review should address the
actual Licensor and markets, particularly commercial restrictions, embedding,
consumer rights, liability and jurisdiction.
